+# Implementation plan
+
+## Premise check
+
+- Saved searches live in browser local storage today
+  (web/reports/saved.ts), so a sign-out on one device or a new device loses them.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. A saved search is stored against the account, not the browser: saving one
+   writes a row to saved_searches keyed by account id, proven by a store test.
+2. After sign-out and sign-in on another device, the reports page lists the
+   account's saved searches in the order they were saved, proven by an API test
+   that saves on one session and lists on a fresh one.
+3. go build ./... and go test ./... pass.
